    "proof": "For primitive r=(x,y), q(r) divides 2I(r), where I(r)=(a*x,(y,Lambda_24)).  The Leech lattice is even unimodular. Thus no prime away from (2) and the squarefree support of a can divide q.  At an odd supported prime P, the valuation is zero or one; the positive case is equivalent to y in P*Lambda_24, and then q=-a*x^2 mod P^2 has valuation exactly one.  At inert (2), an odd coefficient permits valuations zero or one, while v_2(a)=1 forces valuation exactly one by evenness and primitivity.  Class number one and U^+=U^2 leave the displayed canonical totally-positive norms.",
